module Durable
    intent =
        "Forcing bytes already written to a file out to the disk itself,"
        "declared as a contract rather than written."
        "Aver's Disk.appendBytes opens the file, writes and returns. The"
        "bytes are in the operating system's cache at that point and not"
        "necessarily anywhere a power cut cannot take them. That is the right"
        "default for almost everything a program appends -- a log, a report,"
        "a scratch file -- and the wrong one for exactly one thing this"
        "program writes: a Segment whose Location is about to be recorded in"
        "a database that does fsync."
        "n1bor/btc-listener#301 is that pair. The Index batch goes down with"
        "set_sync(true) and returns only once RocksDB's log is on the disk;"
        "the Segment append does not. A power cut between them leaves a"
        "durable b: Location naming bytes that were never written. Infra.Blocks"
        "then truncates the torn tail on the next open and the next download"
        "appends at that offset, so the stale Location names a different"
        "Block's bytes. #283 and #290 made that detectable -- a body is"
        "re-hashed against its Block Id on the way into the Set and on the way"
        "out -- which turned silent corruption into an honest stop asking for"
        "a reindex. This is the other half: keeping the two in step so there"
        "is nothing to detect."
        "A capability and not a Disk call because Aver has no fsync, and a"
        "capability is how Aver says a program needs something the language"
        "does not have -- the same reason Infra.Kv exists. jasisz/aver#1229"
        "asks for Disk.sync upstream; if it lands, this contract retires and"
        "Infra.Blocks calls the effect instead. The provider is"
        "providers/durable, thirty lines of std::fs."
        "The batch form only, like Infra.Kv's: one call names every Segment"
        "that has been appended to since the last one. A batch of Locations"
        "can span a Segment boundary, so the caller that has to make one"
        "batch durable frequently has to make two files durable, and having"
        "only this form is what stops it writing the loop."
        "Nothing here can be checked by aver verify. Whether an fsync reached"
        "the platter is not a claim Aver can evaluate; it is tested in the"
        "provider's own language, against a real file on a real disk."
    kind = capability
    semantics = effectful
    exposes [synced]
    depends []

operation synced(paths: List<String>) -> Result<Unit, String>
    ? "Return once every one of these files is on the disk, or say which one"
      "would not go."
      "A path that does not exist is an error rather than a silence: the"
      "caller names files it has just appended to, so an absent one means the"
      "append did not go where it thought and the Location about to be"
      "written would be wrong."
    oracle = generativeOutput
    replay = recorded
